  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A nitrogen-14 nucleus is bombarded with an alpha particle, resulting in the formation of an oxygen-17 nucleus and the emission of a single particle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span>, as shown in the following nuclear equation:</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"{}^{14}_{7}\\text{N} + {}^{4}_{2}\\text{He} \\rightarrow {}^{17}_{8}\\text{O} + X\"></span></p>\n<p>What is particle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">A neutron</li><li data-label=\"B\">A proton</li><li data-label=\"C\">An electron</li><li data-label=\"D\">A positron</li></ol>"
  },
